  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-09-14T18:44:51.641Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "A New VRC+ tab was recently placed right between the audio and regular options tabs on the quick menu. Please, this really needs to be moved. I don't mind if you guys want to promote a way to sustain your game through paid service but please don't put it right between the two utility items that are very commonly clicked to adjust settings in a game where you must constantly be adjusting settings due to the high variability of user created content. \n\nI cannot think of a single other product that has a completely unrelated menu item or better yet, a premium purchase choice option, wedged in between audio and video/game options. That really doesn't make any sense from a design or practicality standpoint. And from a psychological standpoint, I don't think a missclick strategy while users are trying to change settings, usually due to a negative experience (loud audio, FPS lag->Turning on diamond mode culling) bringing them to the vrc+ menu instead is a good idea. That would just garner negative customer sentiment. Ie* I don't think people wanna missclick and go to a VRC+ begging screen when they are rushing to turn down screamer audio or are stuck at 5fps.\n\nPlease move to somewhere, anywhere else, thanks.",
